# SCG Platform — Task List

## Architecture

The platform IS the product. All resolution and profile queries go through the platform.
The CLI never calls GitHub, Docker Hub, PyPI, or npm directly.

```
scg check → api.scg.bds421.com/v1/resolve  (hash verification)
scg scope → api.scg.bds421.com/v1/profile  (secret scoping)
```

## Platform Infrastructure — DONE

- [x] Platform daemon (scgd) with rho-kit/app, TKG TieredStore
- [x] Marketplace crawler: discovers GitHub Actions, resolves all tags → commit SHAs
- [x] 32,000+ tools indexed from 1,100+ repos
- [x] REST API: /v1/status, /v1/resolve, /v1/profile, /v1/history, /v1/check, /v1/lockfile
- [x] Unauthenticated access (20/hr per IP), authenticated tiers
- [x] Rate limit headers on all responses
- [x] API key auth + per-org rate limiting
- [x] Cron: daily crawl, hourly re-resolve, 15min critical re-resolve
- [x] Drift detection + webhook alerts
- [x] Deployed at api.scg.bds421.com

## CLI Integration — DONE

- [x] `scg check` queries platform for hashes (no GITHUB_TOKEN needed)
- [x] `scg scope` queries platform for profiles (no local graph)
- [x] `scg init` resolves via platform
- [x] No local resolvers in CLI. No fallback.
- [x] Response caching (5 min TTL)
- [x] Landing page at scg.bds421.com with BDS421 branding

